# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Source site-map / floor-plan PDFs downloaded by scripts/nhs/fetch-plans.mjs.
# These are the trusts' copyright, so the repo records where each one came from
# (data/plan-sources.json) and ships only the derived SVGs the app needs, rather
# than mirroring the originals.
#
# The pattern is anchored and wildcarded because a real commit nearly shipped a
# folder called "map- GOSH" holding 40-odd HEIC photos and a video — /map/ alone
# does not match it, and photographs taken inside a children's hospital are the
# last thing that should land in a public repo by accident.
/map*/

# Scratch output of the ingestion pipeline. Every one of these is rebuilt by
# `npm run nhs:all` from data the scripts fetch themselves, so committing them
# adds hundreds of megabytes that go stale immediately.
#
# NOT ignored, because the app or the pipeline reads them as INPUT:
#   mapped-sites.json     the sheet register the venues are built from
#   plan-sources.json     where each PDF came from, for attribution
#   known-maps.json, hospital-aliases.json, venue-aliases.json — hand-written
#   raw/ods/etr.csv       the trust list, small and stable
/data/nhs-sites.json
/data/footprints.geojson
/data/geocode-cache.json
/data/mapped-coverage.json
/data/plan-rejected.json
/data/raw/ods/ets.csv

# Preview thumbnails: a review aid, regenerated on every run, never read by the
# app. "prevnode" is the same thing under a mistyped path.
/data/previews/
/data/prev*/

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but do commit the template (no secrets in it)
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
